## Changes Made
1. Added #include <linux/pkt_cls.h> for TC_ACT_OK/SHOT constants
2. Added #include <linux/if_ether.h> for ethhdr/ETH_P_IP
3. Added #include <linux/udp.h> for udphdr
4. Added #include <linux/tcp.h> for tcphdr
5. Added #include <linux/icmp.h> for icmphdr
6. Defined BPF-side structs (heartbeat, peer_key, authorization, health_state, locked_health)
   — separate from kernel_gate_transition.h header to avoid glibc conflicts
7. Fixed ICMP_ECHOREQUEST → ICMP_ECHO (correct Linux constant)
8. Used bpf_helpers.h libbpf patterns (bpf_skb_load_bytes, bpf_map_lookup_elem, bpf_spin_lock)
9. Removed health_transition function (user-space only)
10. Moved all map-dependent code into .bpf.c

## Map Layout (verified via DWARF/objdump)
- health_map: ARRAY<__u32, health_state>, max 1 entry, key 0
  → health_state has: revision, generation, auth_deadline, epoch, checked, deadline, closed, resource, port, flags
- renewal_state: HASH<peer_key, locked_health>, max 256 entries
  → peer_key = {peer, resource, port, flags}
  → locked_health = {spinlock, health_state}
- auth_map: HASH<peer_key, authorization>, max 256 entries
  → authorization = {epoch, deadline_ns, peer, resource, port, flags}
- verdict_map: ARRAY<__u32, __s32>, max 1 entry

## BPF Programs (3 sections)
1. tc/health_control: Health-control packet classifier
   - Reads packet headers (eth+ip), loads operation/epoch/auth_deadline/deadline fields
   - Validates epoch progression, auth_deadline > deadline, state not closed
   - Updates health_map on success, returns TC_ACT_OK/SHOT

2. tc/wg_ingress: WireGuard ingress classifier (UDP/51820)
   - Validates IPv4/UDP, non-zero source port
   - Checks peer state from renewal_state (spinlock-protected)
   - Validates auth_deadline/health_deadline, resource/port/flags non-zero
   - resource==RESOURCE_PORT, port==WG_PORT

3. tc/resource_ingress: Multi-protocol health port classifier
   - Handles TCP (auth/health/resource ports), UDP (non-zero src), ICMP (echo/reply)
   - Validates peer state from renewal_state
   - Returns TC_ACT_OK if authorized

## Helper Calls (verified in bytecode)
- bpf_map_lookup_elem (helper 1): 3 map lookups (health_map, renewal_state ×2)
- bpf_skb_load_bytes (helper 26): 6+ packet data reads
- bpf_ktime_get_boot_ns (helper 125): 1 call per wg_ingress/resource_ingress
- bpf_spin_lock/unlock: 2 calls per wg_ingress/resource_ingress

